            "review_title": "Review at Smoothies & Juices",
            "review_text": "commedesenfants\n25 contributions\n0\nHidden in plain sight\nSep 2017\nWe saw the café from the street but couldn't see the entrance. We nearly walked by, but saw a sign that explained that you have to walk into the clothing store on the first floor and then take a \"hidden\" elevator up to the first floor. There you get a great view of the lake and the street below. Maybe it's because the cafe is a bit hidden, it was not as crowded with people like the other cafés on the same street, so you can easily get a spot by the window. \n\nParticularly on weekends when the street below is only open to pedestrians, it's great for people watching. The smoothies are delicious (we had the mango, avocado and coconut smoohie) and relatively cheap especially if you consider the prime location. The interior design is also lovely. \n\nI can definitely recommend this place to anyone who got tired from walking along the lake and the old quarter and wants to get a break.\nRead more\nWritten September 16, 2017",
